Billy, played by Jared Rushton.

11
00:57:12,000 --> 00:57:18,000
Young Josh, played by David Moscow.

12
01:02:24,000 --> 01:02:30,000
Big is a 1988 American fantasy comedy film directed by Penny Marshall and starring Tom Hanks as Josh
Baskin, an adolescent boy whose wish to be "big" transforms him physically into an adult.

13
01:07:36,000 --> 01:07:42,000
The film also stars Elizabeth Perkins, David Moscow, John Heard, and Robert
Loggia, and was written by Gary Ross and Anne Spielberg.

14
01:12:48,000 --> 01:12:54,000
It was produced by Gracie Films and distributed by 20th Century Fox.

15
01:18:00,000 --> 01:18:06,000
Upon release, Big was met with wide critical acclaim,
particularly for Hanks' performance.

16
01:23:12,000 --> 01:23:18,000
It was a huge commercial success as well, grossing $151 million worldwide against a production budget of $18 million, and it
proved to be pivotal to Hanks' career, establishing him as a major box-office draw as well as a critical favorite.

17
01:28:24,000 --> 01:28:30,000
The film received Academy Award nominations for Best
Actor (Hanks) and Best Original Screenplay.

18
01:33:36,000 --> 01:33:42,000
The film explores themes of baseball, coming of age, best
friend, co-workers relationship, body-swap.

19
01:38:48,000 --> 01:38:54,000
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
